## Standard Test Scenarios

### Required Test Scenarios
Every operation SHOULD have tests for the following scenarios:

| Scenario | Tag | Status Code | Description |
|----------|-----|-------------|-------------|
| Success | `SUCCESS` | 200/201 | Happy path validation |
| Connectivity Error | `ERROR` | 500 | Backend system connectivity failure |
| Partial Success | `PARTIAL SUCCESS` | 200/207 | Mixed results in batch/composite operations |
| Validation Error | `ERROR` | 400 | Input validation failures |
| Not Found | `ERROR` | 404 | Resource not found scenarios |
| Service Error | `ERROR` | 500 | Backend service errors (timeouts, faults) |

### Test Tags
Use `tags` attribute for categorization:
```xml
<munit:test name="..." tags="SUCCESS">
<munit:test name="..." tags="ERROR">
<munit:test name="..." tags="PARTIAL SUCCESS">
```

## Assertion Patterns

### Assert Equals
```xml
<munit-tools:assert-equals doc:name="Assert Response" 
                           actual="#[payload]" 
                           expected="#[output application/json --- readUrl('classpath://testdata/{suite}/business-outbound/{operation}-success-response.json')]"/>
```

### Assert That with Matchers
```xml
<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[vars.httpStatus]" 
                         is="#[MunitTools::equalTo(200)]" 
                         message="Expected HTTP status 200"/>

<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[payload]" 
                         is="#[MunitTools::notNullValue()]"/>

<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[payload.errors[0].code]" 
                         is="#[MunitTools::containsString('ERR')]"/>

<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[sizeOf(payload.items)]" 
                         is="#[MunitTools::greaterThan(0)]"/>
```

### Verify Call Count
```xml
<munit-tools:verify-call processor="mule:flow-ref" times="1" doc:name="Verify Flow Called Once">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute attributeName="name" whereValue="{flow-name}"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
</munit-tools:verify-call>
```

## Common Patterns and Best Practices

### 1. Test Isolation
- Each test should be independent
- Mock all external dependencies
- Don't rely on execution order

### 2. Descriptive Names
Use clear, descriptive names for all test components:
```xml
<munit:set-event doc:name="Set Create Order Request Payload"/>
<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock Backend Order Service Response"/>
<munit-tools:assert-that doc:name="Assert Order Created Successfully"/>
```

### 3. Comprehensive Assertions
Always assert:
- HTTP status code (`vars.httpStatus`)
- Response payload structure
- Technical inbound payloads (via spies)
- Flow/processor call verification

### 4. Reusable Test Data
For common mocks, store in a shared location:
```
src/test/resources/testdata/common/
├── empty-response.json
├── connectivity-error-response.json
└── validation-error-response.json
```

## Quick Reference Checklist

When implementing a new MUnit test, ensure:

- [ ] Test suite file name follows pattern: `{operation}-test-suite.xml`
- [ ] Test case names follow pattern: `{prefix}-{operation}-{scenario}-test-suite`
- [ ] Testdata directory structure is created with all four folders
- [ ] All testdata files use proper naming: `{operation}-{scenario}-{type}.{extension}`
- [ ] `readUrl()` is wrapped with `output application/json ---` (or appropriate format)
- [ ] All external services are mocked
- [ ] Spies are configured for outbound calls (if needed)
- [ ] HTTP status code is asserted
- [ ] Response payload is asserted
- [ ] Success scenario is implemented with tag `SUCCESS`
- [ ] Error scenarios are implemented with tag `ERROR`
- [ ] Test data files are properly formatted
- [ ] Tests are independent and isolated
- [ ] All `doc:name` attributes are descriptive

